storytold-vectorcraft (0.24.1-1~smallgearlab1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of VectorCraft 0.24.1, an open-source vector illustration
    app written in Rust (storytold/vectorcraft), from the upstream release tag.
  * Built offline with the local rustup toolchain from the crates that
    build.sh vendored.
  * Two packages, split as storytold-photocraft is: storytold-vectorcraft (the
    editor window) and storytold-vectorcraft-cli (the headless converter,
    command runner and MCP server). The packages carry the storytold prefix of
    their upstream organisation; the programs keep their names
    (/usr/bin/vectorcraft, /usr/bin/vectorcraft-cli). The CLI has no windowing
    or GPU dependencies; the editor recommends it. HEIC/HEIF support is built in
    (a default feature of the engine).
  * The CLI has no man page generator or shell completions upstream, so its
    man page is written here (debian/vectorcraft-cli.1).
  * debian/copyright: gen-crate-licenses.py writes a paragraph for each Rust
    crate that is linked in, and the .docs files install the license files of
    those crates and of the bundled fonts, icons and PDF backend data.

 -- small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0900
